                <pb facs="0188" n="86" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg86"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/169–173.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-04-14"><hi rendition="#italic">April 14,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The department received in due course, and
                    read with gratification, Mr. Fletcher’s dispatch No. 845, of February 14 last,
                    in which he reported that an agreement had been reached between the Governments
                    of Great Britain and China for the suppression of the opium trade between India
                    and China, this desirable end to be obtained within 10 years.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
